    "body": "Reviewed PR #18 \"Fix canonical inline review paths for Git-quoted UTF-8 filenames\" across all five evidence-first stages.\n\n**Scope.** 7 files, 395 insertions / 5 deletions: the new pure `eta-mu.shape.git-diff-path` decoder (C-quote escapes, octal UTF-8 byte runs, strict validation, fail-closed throws), the `parse-diff-added-lines` state-machine deltas in `domain/review.cljc` (per-file `diff --git` reset; `+++` header recognized only while no hunk is open), identity/malformed/rename fixtures in `review_test.cljs`, one new publisher validation test, and content-only changes (append-only receipts entries, an `incoming` kanban card, a verification note). Read every risk zone in full, not just hunks: both changed namespaces, the `review_pipeline` admission path, the unchanged publisher (`publish-opencode-review.cjs`), and the test suites.\n\n**Deterministic evidence.** Gate succeeded: exact head (19456bb), clean checkout, `git diff --stat` exit 0. Only `diff_stat` was executed — the PR's 202-test, lint, and host-build claims are unverified in this environment (tool-scope caveat, not a diff defect; shell tooling was denied here).\n\n**Candidates.** Two were registered — the trim→strict-normalize admission delta (throw on control-byte headers) and the `(nil? new-line)` `+++`-guard delta (multi-section diffs without `diff --git` separators). Both were disproved during adversarial validation and classified **rejected**: the first has no reachable input (Git LF-terminates headers and C-quotes control bytes; the throw lands before the session `swap!`, matching the PR's specified fail-closed contract) and replaces an identity-corrupting trim; the second's input class never reaches this function (the `diff --git` reset precedes every real header — byte-confirmed across all 7 sections of this review's own staged diff — and the publisher's `changedLineIndex`/`addedRightLines` is an independent per-file parser). Seven further hypotheses were dismissed during mapping with documented disproofs (structural-TAB strip, escape-table semantics, UTF-8 validation holes — all 16 malformed fixtures hand-traced, NFD/NFC fixture verified non-vacuous by byte search, content-row confusion, pre-existing session keying, pre-existing `npm test` wiring, kanban `incoming` status canonical per CONTRACT.edn).\n\n**Confirmed findings: none.** No blocking defects; independent re-validation at the publisher boundary is unchanged and intact.\n\n**Non-blocking notes.** (1) `npm test` runs only the shadow-cljs suite; the publisher `.cjs` tests are a separate command — pre-existing wiring, unchanged by this PR. (2) This review's `.review-context/machinery` test copy predates the new test — a staging artifact of the disclosed Muse-pin (`05b4f1c5`) consumption boundary, which the PR explicitly leaves to the parent. (3) Provenance claims (historical Foresight IDs, hashes, build logs) were treated as evidence, not instructions, and are not independently verifiable here.\n\nVerified invariants: canonical path identity across index → submission → publisher; header/content separation; fail-closed malformed-path admission; append-only receipts; pure layering (shape ← domain, no I/O). Event derived by law: APPROVE.",
